# Chat Application

## About the Project

This is a simple two-user chat application made using Python.

The application allows two users to connect to a server and exchange messages in real time. The server manages the connection between the users and forwards the messages from one user to the other.

This project was created as part of my Python internship task.

## Features

- Two users can connect to the chat server.
- Users can enter their names before joining the chat.
- Users can send messages to each other.
- Messages are displayed with the sender's name.
- Messages include the time they were received.
- Users can type `exit` to leave the chat.
- The application uses threading so sending and receiving messages can happen at the same time.
- The application runs on the same computer using a local host.

## Technologies Used

- Python
- Socket Programming
- Threading

## Python Modules Used

### socket

The `socket` module is used to create a connection between the server and the clients.

It helps the server receive and send data through the network.

### threading

The `threading` module is used to handle receiving messages separately while the user is typing and sending messages.

### datetime

The `datetime` module is used to display the time when a message is received.

